    "competency_fulfillment": {
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "rationale": "Seventeen of eighteen items are correct subtraction with the stated result, for example seed 502 with 'What is 96 − 91?' keyed 5, and seed 50 with 'The total is 75 and one part is 15. What is the other part?' keyed 60. Seed 500 is unanswerable: the whole prompt is 'How many items are left?' with no quantity, no picture content and no starting amount, yet it keys 33 against distractors 32, 66 and 165. Nothing in the sample lets a student reach that value."
    },
    "comprehensive_coverage": {
      "verdict": "CONCERN",
      "rationale": "Both named sub cases are present. Two digit minus one digit appears at seed 604 with 'What is 13 − 1?', seed 82 with 'Dante says: 21 − 1 = 20. Is Dante correct?' and seed 605 with 'The total is 24 and one part is 1. What is the other part?'. Two digit minus two digit appears at seed 44 with '60 − 50 = ___', seed 501 with '89 − 14 = 75. True or False?' and seed 45. The concrete and pictorial models the sentence also names are close to missing. Only seed 51 models anything, with 'The dot is at 36 and it moves backward 15 numbers.', and the single picture slot at seed 500 renders with no content."
    },
    "cognitive_capacity": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "The symbolic form is short and readable for Grade 1 Quarter 3, and the two word framings stay at one step: seed 601 reads 'Pia has 25 leashes.' before asking how many more, and seed 605 uses a plain total and part sentence. No multi step chaining, no unfamiliar vocabulary and no distracting extra information appears in any of the eighteen samples."
    },
    "variant_comprehensiveness": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "Six response modes appear across the eighteen seeds: multiple choice, cloze equation at seed 603 with '22 − 20 = ___', true or false at seed 75, error detection at seed 82, picture based choice at seed 51 and a fill in response at seed 50. Presentation also varies between the question form 'What is 40 − 10?' and the equation form."
    },
    "competency_alignment": {
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "rationale": "The without regrouping restriction holds in every sample I checked. In each pair the ones digit of the minuend is at least the ones digit of the subtrahend: 96 and 91, 89 and 14, 75 and 15, 36 and 15, 66 and 60, 24 and 1, 22 and 20, 25 and 15, and the decade pairs at seed 45 with '40 − 30 = ___' and seed 602. No item requires borrowing, and no addition or later operation is introduced."
    },
